.TH BUSH-TASKS 1 "2026-09-12" "bush-tasks 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bush-tasks \- a small cross-platform CLI task manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bush-tasks
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bush-tasks
is an interactive command-line task manager. It stores tasks in a JSON file
.RB ( tasks.json )
in the current working directory.
.PP
Run
.B bush-tasks
without arguments to start the interactive loop. Type
.B exit
to quit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI add " text"
Add a new task with the given text.
.TP
.BI del " number"
Delete the task with the given 1-based number.
.TP
.BI edit " number text"
Replace the text of the task with the given number.
.TP
.BI sub " number text"
Add a subtask to the task with the given number.
.TP
.BI priority " number level"
Change the priority of a task. Level must be one of:
.BR low ,
.BR medium ,
.B high ,
or
.BR urgent .
.TP
.BI status " number state"
Change the status of a task. State must be one of:
.BR pending ,
.BR done ,
or
.BR postponed .
.TP
.B tasks
List all tasks.
.TP
.B clear
Delete all tasks.
.TP
.BR exit " or " quit
Exit the program.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I tasks.json
The task database. Created automatically on first save.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Add a task:
.RS
.EX
> add Write documentation
Task added
.EE
.RE
.TP
Change its priority:
.RS
.EX
> priority 1 high
Priority updated
.EE
.RE
.TP
Mark it done:
.RS
.EX
> status 1 done
Status updated
.EE
.RE
